{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":343027,"duration_api_ms":341651,"num_turns":49,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"b5a475ab-2daf-4787-9ca4-63ce2630cf4d","total_cost_usd":2.2151605,"usage":{"input_tokens":36,"cache_creation_input_tokens":96786,"cache_read_input_tokens":2660586,"output_tokens":11191,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":96786,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":36,"outputTokens":11191,"cacheReadInputTokens":2660586,"cacheCreationInputTokens":96786,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":2.2151605,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"amendments":[{"body":"In `molt_mineral_modifier` (shrimp.rs:1405) and `update_molt_stress` (shrimp.rs:451), `params.gh_min_d` is used as a divisor without a `.max(0.01)` guard. The invariant on `gh_min_d` (invariants.rs:332) uses `check_non_negative`, which allows `0.0`. This creates a division-by-zero path that produces NaN/Infinity. The sister functions `gh_mineral_factor` (line 1355) and `critical_gh_deficit` (line 517) correctly guard with `.max(0.01)`. Fix: either change the invariant to `check_positive` for `gh_min_d`, or add `.max(0.01)` to the two unguarded division sites.","rationale":"If a user or data file ever sets `gh_min_d = 0.0` (which passes current validation), `molt_mineral_modifier` returns NaN that propagates through molt success scoring and `update_molt_stress` produces NaN in the molt stress index. Both can silently corrupt downstream mortality calculations. The inconsistency with the guarded call sites in the same file suggests this was an oversight."}],"summary":"The mineral budget and molt mechanics implementation is solid: all 14 tests pass, covering GH monotonicity, Ca/Mg contribution, condition effects, mortality from failed molts, named parameter tunability, stage-specific molt frequency, and the integration soft-vs-hard-water survival test. Event diagnostics clearly surface GH, Ca, Mg, temperature, reserve, and condition causes. All thresholds and modifiers live in `ShrimpRuntimeParams` with serde defaults and invariant validation. The one real issue is two unguarded division-by-`gh_min_d` sites that can produce NaN if the parameter is 0.0 — a value the current invariant allows."},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"9c9a6bfa-ec16-47d5-8b56-dba64c5ed5a5"}
